        '6-8', $q$Letters to Valentina$q$, $q$(1) This year, our seventh-grade class started writing letters to students at a school in a small town in Chile. (2) Each of us was matched with one partner who was learning English, while we were learning Spanish. (3) In my first letter, I described my family, my dog, and my favorite foods. (4) Three weeks later, a thick envelope arrived from my partner, Valentina. (5) She had written half of her letter in English and half in Spanish so that we could both practice.

(6) Writing to a real person changed the way I learn. (7) Before the project, I memorized vocabulary lists only to pass quizzes. (8) Now, I look up new words because I want to tell Valentina about my life. (9) Our school cafeteria serves tacos every Tuesday. (10) ____, I have learned more about daily life in Chile from her letters than from any textbook. (11) By June, our letters had become longer, funnier, and much easier to write.$q$, 'draft')
