   $q$Which choice best combines sentences 7 and 8 while keeping the relationship between the ideas clear?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Each one passes through pockets of air that are slightly warmer, colder, wetter, or drier, for example, every change affects how the arms grow.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"example-for-addition"},{"text":"Each one passes through pockets of air that are slightly warmer, colder, wetter, or drier, unless every change affects how the arms grow.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"condition-for-addition"},{"text":"Each one passes through pockets of air that are slightly warmer, colder, wetter, or drier, although every change affects how the arms grow.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contrast-for-addition"},{"text":"Each one passes through pockets of air that are slightly warmer, colder, wetter, or drier, and every change affects how the arms grow.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Each one passes through pockets of air that are slightly warmer, colder, wetter, or drier, and every change affects how the arms grow.$q$, $q$Sentence 8 builds on sentence 7 by explaining what the changing air does, so joining them with "and" keeps the meaning. "Although" is wrong because nothing in sentence 8 goes against sentence 7.$q$, 'draft', 'b29390a6-cef7-55b0-b93f-e32aff1127e5')
