   $q$Read the sentences: (A) Next, she found the hole and covered it with a patch. (B) Imani took the flat tire off her bike and pulled out the inner tube. (C) Finally, she pumped up the tire and took a test ride. (D) After the patch dried, she put the tube back inside the tire. Which is the most logical order?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A, B, D, C","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-transition-cues"},{"text":"B, A, C, D","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-finally"},{"text":"B, D, A, C","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-transition-cues"},{"text":"B, A, D, C","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$B, A, D, C$q$, $q$Imani must remove the tube first, then patch it ("Next"), then put it back after the patch dries, and pump it up last ("Finally"). Order B, D, A, C is wrong because sentence D mentions a patch that has dried before the patch is added in sentence A.$q$, 'draft', null)
