   $q$A student writes a speech for the student council: "Our school's recycling bins are, like, kind of always full and stuff." The student knows the bins overflow by every Wednesday. Which revision best fits a formal speech and is the most precise?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Our recycling bins are always full and stuff, which is bad.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"informal-filler"},{"text":"Our recycling bins are, like, always really full.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"informal-filler"},{"text":"Our school's recycling bins are kind of full a lot of the time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-modifier"},{"text":"Our school's recycling bins overflow by every Wednesday.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Our school's recycling bins overflow by every Wednesday.$q$, $q$"Overflow by every Wednesday" is formal and tells exactly how full the bins get and when. The choice "Our school's recycling bins are kind of full a lot of the time" drops the slang but keeps vague words like "kind of" and "a lot of the time."$q$, 'draft', null)
