   $q$Which sentence is a run-on?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The fair opened at noon. Crowds filled the midway by one.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"two-sentences-as-run-on"},{"text":"The fair opened at noon, and crowds filled the midway by one.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"compound-as-run-on"},{"text":"The fair opened at noon crowds filled the midway by one.","is_correct":true},{"text":"When the fair opened at noon, crowds filled the midway.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"complex-as-run-on"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The fair opened at noon crowds filled the midway by one.$q$, $q$"The fair opened at noon" and "crowds filled the midway by one" are two independent clauses with no punctuation or conjunction between them, which is a run-on. The choice "The fair opened at noon, and crowds filled the midway by one" joins the same clauses correctly with a comma and "and."$q$, 'draft', null)
