   $q$Read the words: "Whenever Hana visits the aquarium." Which statement best describes this group of words?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It is a compound sentence with two independent clauses.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misidentifies-as-compound"},{"text":"It is a complete simple sentence with a subject and a verb.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"subordinator-ignored"},{"text":"It is a fragment because it is a dependent clause standing alone.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It is a run-on because it needs a comma after \"Hana.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misidentifies-as-run-on"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It is a fragment because it is a dependent clause standing alone.$q$, $q$The word "Whenever" makes the clause dependent, so the reader is left asking what happens whenever Hana visits. Having a subject and a verb is not enough when a subordinating word leaves the thought unfinished.$q$, 'draft', null)
