   $q$Read the sentence: "The recipe called for fresh basil ___ we used dried basil instead." Which choice correctly completes the sentence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"basil, however, we","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"conjunctive-adverb-with-comma"},{"text":"basil, however; we","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reversed-punctuation"},{"text":"basil however we","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fused-sentence"},{"text":"basil; however, we","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$basil; however, we$q$, $q$"However" is not a coordinating conjunction, so when it joins two independent clauses it needs a semicolon before it and a comma after it. Commas on both sides of "however" still leave a comma splice.$q$, 'draft', null)
