  ('0216e71a-4548-59c1-8b77-f909308ccb7a', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g7-sentence-structure'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Read the words: "The old lighthouse on the rocky point near the harbor." This group of words is a fragment. What does it need to become a complete sentence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"a coordinating conjunction such as \"and\" or \"but\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"conjunction-as-fix"},{"text":"a subject that names what the sentence is about","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-existing-subject"},{"text":"a verb that tells what the lighthouse does or is","is_correct":true},{"text":"a semicolon to separate the two phrases","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"punctuation-as-fix"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$a verb that tells what the lighthouse does or is$q$, $q$"The old lighthouse" is already a subject, followed by two prepositional phrases, but there is no verb, so adding one (such as "still guides ships") completes the sentence. The subject is present, so adding another subject would not help.$q$, 'draft', null)
