   $q$Which sentence contains two independent clauses joined by a comma and a coordinating conjunction?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The scientists and the students collected samples and recorded temperatures.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"compound-subject-as-compound"},{"text":"While the scientists collected samples, the students recorded the temperatures.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"complex-as-compound"},{"text":"The scientists collected water samples and tested them for pollution.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"compound-predicate-as-compound"},{"text":"The scientists collected water samples, and the students recorded the temperatures.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The scientists collected water samples, and the students recorded the temperatures.$q$, $q$"The scientists collected water samples" and "the students recorded the temperatures" each have their own subject and verb, and they are joined by a comma and "and." The choice "The scientists collected water samples and tested them for pollution" has two verbs but only one subject, so it is a single clause.$q$, 'draft', null)
