        '6-8', $q$Draft: Where Did the Fireflies Go?$q$, $q$(1) In the article "Lights Out for Fireflies," Priya Desai explains why fireflies are harder to find in many neighborhoods than they used to be. (2) I remember catching fireflies in a jar at my cousin's house every July. (3) Desai writes that fireflies use their flashing lights to find each other at night. (4) She reports that in one study, "fireflies in brightly lit yards flashed about half as often as fireflies in dark fields." (5) This means bright lights make it harder for fireflies to send signals to each other.

(6) ____, Desai points out that fireflies spend most of their lives as larvae in damp soil and leaf piles. (7) When people rake away every leaf and mow their lawns very short, the larvae lose their hiding places. (8) Desai notes that one park left a strip of tall grass and leaves alone, and the number of fireflies there doubled in three summers. (9) This example shows that giving larvae a safe place to grow can help bring fireflies back.

(10) Fireflies are really cool bugs.$q$, 'draft')
