   $q$Which revision of sentence 11 would best conclude the draft?$q$, $q$[{"text":"This story is about a girl named Rosa who is a swimmer on a team.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-claim"},{"text":"Swimming is a good sport because it keeps people strong and healthy.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-fact"},{"text":"Okafor writes that Rosa \"had something left, and she used every bit of it.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"evidence-without-analysis"},{"text":"Rosa's change from sprinting early to pacing herself shows that patience helped her swim her fastest race.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Rosa's change from sprinting early to pacing herself shows that patience helped her swim her fastest race.$q$, $q$The choice about "sprinting early to pacing herself" ties the beginning and end of the story back to the claim about patience. Repeating the quotation from sentence 8 gives evidence again but does not sum up what it shows.$q$, 'draft', '0d44d488-c958-5083-8b9b-f1803d3da879')
