  ('47281944-5e59-5595-9619-d591da39fdd5', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g7-writing-with-evidence'), null, 'hard',
   $q$A classmate says sentence 10 weakens the draft because Rosa does not win. Which response best explains why sentence 10 actually supports the claim?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The claim is about swimming her best race, and cutting four seconds shows that pacing made her faster.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Finishing second shows that the rival team must have broken the rules of the meet.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Finishing second shows that Mr. Halvorsen gave Rosa poor advice about saving energy.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-text"},{"text":"Finishing second proves that Rosa's new plan failed and she should go back to sprinting.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-claim"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The claim is about swimming her best race, and cutting four seconds shows that pacing made her faster.$q$, $q$Sentence 1 says patience helps Rosa swim "her best race," not win, so a new best time is strong support. Nothing in the draft suggests the plan failed, since she improved by four seconds.$q$, 'draft', '0d44d488-c958-5083-8b9b-f1803d3da879')
