insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('32c27476-9174-52e9-8910-68cf08a3b31b', 'wg7-writing-with-evidence-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g7-writing-with-evidence'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Draft: A Song Passed Down$q$, $q$(1) In the story "The Steel Pan," by Celeste Moreau, a boy named Darnell learns to play the steel pan from his grandfather. (2) ____. (3) At first, Darnell finds the old instrument boring and would rather play video games. (4) Moreau writes that Grandpa "played the same song every evening, the one his own father had taught him." (5) This detail shows that the song has been passed down through the family for many years.

(6) As the story goes on, Darnell begins to practice the song himself. (7) He makes many mistakes, but Grandpa only laughs and says, "My notes were worse." (8) Moreau writes that by the end of summer, the two of them "played side by side, and nobody could tell whose notes were whose." (9) Steel pans are made from large metal drums. (10) The steel pan becomes a way for Darnell and Grandpa to understand each other.$q$, 'draft')
