   $q$Which detail from the article would best fill blank (4)?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Haddad notes that the bakery near the old station doubled its customers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misplaced-evidence"},{"text":"Haddad notes that many neighbors called the area an eyesore and avoided walking near it.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Haddad notes that bike helmets now come in many different sizes and colors.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-fact"},{"text":"Haddad notes that the old trains were painted dark red with gold letters.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-evidence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Haddad notes that many neighbors called the area an eyesore and avoided walking near it.$q$, $q$Sentence 3 describes the land before the trail, and a detail about neighbors avoiding the eyesore adds to that picture of the problem. The bakery detail is real evidence, but it shows the results after the trail opened and is already used in sentence 8.$q$, 'draft', '50dc02b2-2fe4-545a-9de0-3cc18dbbe6be')
