   $q$Why should the writer remove sentence 10?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It is the strongest example of how the trail helped older residents.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misjudges-evidence"},{"text":"It is the main claim of the draft, so it belongs at the beginning instead.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misidentifies-claim"},{"text":"It repeats the quotation about the bakery that appears in sentence 8.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-repetition"},{"text":"It gives a general fact about trains instead of showing how people use the trail today.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It gives a general fact about trains instead of showing how people use the trail today.$q$, $q$Paragraph 2 lists examples of how the trail is used now, and a fact about old train travel does not fit that list. Sentence 10 says nothing about the bakery or older residents.$q$, 'draft', '50dc02b2-2fe4-545a-9de0-3cc18dbbe6be')
