   $q$The writer wants to add a sentence after sentence 8 to explain the quotation. Which sentence works best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"This shows that summer is the busiest season for every business in the country.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralizes"},{"text":"This shows that people using the trail also spend money at the shops along it.","is_correct":true},{"text":"This shows that the bakery is located close to where the old station stood.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"restates-evidence"},{"text":"This shows that the bakery near the station makes the best bread in Millbrook.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$This shows that people using the trail also spend money at the shops along it.$q$, $q$The quotation shows the bakery got more customers once the trail opened, which supports the claim that the trail helped local shops. Saying the bakery is near the station only repeats part of the quotation without explaining why it matters.$q$, 'draft', '50dc02b2-2fe4-545a-9de0-3cc18dbbe6be')
