   $q$Which ending best completes sentence 5?$q$, $q$[{"text":"fish are not able to see any colors at all when they swim past.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"an octopus can match its surroundings fast enough to stay hidden from passing fish.","is_correct":true},{"text":"octopuses like resting on spotted rocks more than on any other kind of rock.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"an octopus's skin has thousands of tiny color cells inside it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"restates-evidence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$an octopus can match its surroundings fast enough to stay hidden from passing fish.$q$, $q$The quotation shows the octopus changes before the fish arrives, so the explanation should be about hiding quickly. Saying the skin has thousands of color cells only repeats sentence 3 instead of explaining the quotation.$q$, 'draft', '1971d341-5ee0-5d6e-97b8-40807ee701fe')
