   $q$Which detail would best support the reason given in sentences (6) and (7)?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The empty lot on Elm Street has stood vacant for nearly ten years.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"supports-different-point"},{"text":"Tomatoes grow best when they receive at least six hours of sunlight each day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-detail"},{"text":"At a garden in a nearby town, more than 40 neighbors attend monthly work days, and many had never met before.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Some neighbors would rather buy their vegetables at the weekend farmers market.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"undermines-claim"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$At a garden in a nearby town, more than 40 neighbors attend monthly work days, and many had never met before.$q$, $q$Sentences (6) and (7) argue that a garden brings people together, and the correct detail shows neighbors meeting through a garden. The detail about the lot being vacant is true background but does not show people coming together.$q$, 'draft', '73c2e641-b660-5dd5-bb56-eb9ec49cbafc')
