   $q$Which revision of sentence (11) provides the best formal conclusion?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Refill stations are a thing that a lot of schools have.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-wording"},{"text":"Anyway, that is about all I have to say about water.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"no-restated-claim"},{"text":"So yeah, refill stations would be totally awesome for real.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"keeps-informal-tone"},{"text":"By installing refill stations, the district can cut plastic waste and help students stay focused.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$By installing refill stations, the district can cut plastic waste and help students stay focused.$q$, $q$The correct revision is formal and restates both reasons from the essay, waste and focus. The other choices are casual or vague and do not follow from the argument.$q$, 'draft', '8f8fdcce-3cf8-5a35-9d02-cbb7d2a40f51')
