   $q$Sentence (6) makes a statement without support. Which sentence, added after it, provides the most relevant evidence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A university study found that students who drank water during tests scored higher than those who did not.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Many students prefer sports drinks to plain water.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"undermines-claim"},{"text":"Water covers most of the surface of Earth.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-detail"},{"text":"The cafeteria sells bottled water for one dollar.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"supports-different-point"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A university study found that students who drank water during tests scored higher than those who did not.$q$, $q$The study links drinking water to better performance, which directly supports the idea that hydrated students concentrate better. The fact about sports drinks does not support sentence (6) and even weakens the second reason.$q$, 'draft', '8f8fdcce-3cf8-5a35-9d02-cbb7d2a40f51')
