insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('4c9242a6-9423-5b80-bd3b-b16f6c491320', 'wg8-argument-writing-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g8-argument-writing'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Wildflowers Instead of Lawn$q$, $q$(1) Behind Cedar Hill Middle School lies a wide lawn that the grounds crew mows every week from April to October. (2) The school should replace part of this lawn with a garden of native wildflowers and grasses. (3) Native plants support local wildlife. (4) Bees, butterflies, and birds depend on these plants for food and shelter, and many of these animals are becoming harder to find. (5) A native garden would also save the school money. (6) Because native plants are adapted to the local climate, they need little watering and no weekly mowing. (7) The grounds crew estimates that shrinking the lawn by half would cut mowing costs by about $3,000 a year.

(8) Some teachers worry that a wild garden would look messy. (9) A garden with clear paths, signs, and neatly edged borders can look just as tidy as a lawn. (10) Science classes could also use the garden as an outdoor classroom to study insects and plant life. (11) I saw a really pretty butterfly last summer at the beach.

(12) A lawn may look neat, but it does very little for the school or the environment.$q$, 'draft')
