   $q$The teacher means that only the students who finish early may read. Which sentence is punctuated correctly for that meaning?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Students, who finish the lab early, may read quietly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"restrictive-clause-set-off"},{"text":"Students who finish, the lab early may read quietly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splits-clause"},{"text":"Students who finish the lab early may read quietly.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Students who finish the lab early, may read quietly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-between-subject-verb"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Students who finish the lab early may read quietly.$q$, $q$The clause "who finish the lab early" tells which students may read, so it is essential and takes no commas. Setting it off with commas would make it sound like all students finish early and all may read.$q$, 'draft', null)
