   $q$Read the original sentence: "Bees visit thousands of flowers each day, and they carry pollen from one plant to the next." A student leaves out "each day." Which shortened quotation correctly marks the omission?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"Bees visit thousands ... of flowers each day, and they carry pollen from one plant to the next.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ellipsis-nothing-omitted"},{"text":"\"Bees visit thousands of flowers ... and they carry pollen from one plant to the next.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"Bees visit thousands of flowers; and they carry pollen from one plant to the next.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-for-omission"},{"text":"\"Bees visit thousands of flowers, and they carry pollen from one plant to the next.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"omission-not-marked"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"Bees visit thousands of flowers ... and they carry pollen from one plant to the next."$q$, $q$The ellipsis appears exactly where "each day" was removed. The choice with a plain comma drops the words without telling the reader anything is missing.$q$, 'draft', null)
