   $q$Read the sentence: "We drove North for two days to visit relatives in the southwest." Which choice correctly describes how to fix the capitalization?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Change \"North\" to \"north\" and \"southwest\" to \"Southwest.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"Change \"southwest\" to \"Southwest\" and leave \"North\" as it is.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"direction-capitalized"},{"text":"Change \"North\" to \"north\" and leave \"southwest\" as it is.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"region-lowercased"},{"text":"Leave both words as they are, because both are correct.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"no-error-seen"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Change "North" to "north" and "southwest" to "Southwest."$q$, $q$"North" here is just a direction of travel, so it should be lowercase, while "the Southwest" names a region and should be capitalized. Fixing only one of the two words leaves an error in the sentence.$q$, 'draft', null)
