   $q$Read the sentence: "The coach insists that every player ____ water during practice." Which choice correctly completes the sentence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"drinks","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"indicative-for-subjunctive"},{"text":"drink","is_correct":true},{"text":"drank","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"past-tense-for-subjunctive"},{"text":"will drink","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"future-for-subjunctive"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$drink$q$, $q$After a verb of demand such as "insists that," standard English uses the subjunctive, which is the base form "drink." "Drinks" is the ordinary indicative form and is not used after "insists that."$q$, 'draft', null)
