   $q$Read the sentence: "Jun wishes he ____ taller so he could reach the high shelf." Which choice correctly completes the sentence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"is","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"indicative-after-wish"},{"text":"were","is_correct":true},{"text":"has been","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"perfect-after-wish"},{"text":"will be","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"future-after-wish"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$were$q$, $q$A wish about something untrue in the present takes the subjunctive "were." "Is" states a present fact, which does not fit a wish about something that is not true.$q$, 'draft', null)
