   $q$The writer wants to add a concluding sentence after sentence 13 that sums up the main idea of the report. Which is best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Railroads were the most important invention in the history of the world.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-claim"},{"text":"Although railroads replaced them, canals once linked farms to cities and helped young towns grow.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Today, many families enjoy biking on old towpaths on sunny weekends.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Each lock used a set of gates to move water in and out of a chamber.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"repeats-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Although railroads replaced them, canals once linked farms to cities and helped young towns grow.$q$, $q$The correct choice restates the report's central point, that canals mattered for trade and towns before railroads took over. The towpath sentence only extends the last detail and does not sum up the report.$q$, 'draft', 'a009672a-6be3-5deb-bea8-66030b41d433')
