insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('f70f8e8a-536e-5610-937f-3734e826b7f9', 'wg8-informative-writing-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g8-informative-writing'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Growing Together$q$, $q$(1) Have you ever seen an empty lot turn green? (2) A community garden is a piece of land that neighbors farm together, with each family or group tending its own bed. (3) These gardens give people fresh food, a place to meet, and a chance to learn.

(4) First, community gardens provide fresh vegetables to families who may not have space to garden at home. (5) In the Maple Street garden, twenty families grow tomatoes, beans, peppers, and greens. (6) Last summer, the gardeners also donated extra produce to a local food pantry.

(7) Second, the gardens bring neighbors together. (8) Gardeners share tools, trade seeds, and help each other water during hot weeks. (9) Stuff happens there too, like events. (10) Older residents often teach younger ones how to make compost.

(11) Finally, the gardens help students learn about science. (12) A nearby middle school uses two beds to study soil, insects, and plant growth. (13) My favorite vegetable is corn.$q$, 'draft')
