insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('1e6a63f5-0a13-5cbe-8c4b-0eacccf92614', 'wg8-informative-writing-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g8-informative-writing'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Why Teens Need More Sleep$q$, $q$(1) Many students stay up late and then struggle to wake up for school. (2) Sleep experts recommend that teenagers get about eight to ten hours of sleep each night. (3) However, surveys show that many teens get far less.

(4) One reason is that a teen's body clock changes during puberty. (5) The body clock is the internal system that tells a person when to feel sleepy and when to feel alert. (6) In the teen years, this clock shifts later, so many teens do not feel tired until late at night. (7) Bright screens can make the problem worse, because their light signals the brain that it is still daytime.

(8) Not getting enough sleep affects more than mood. (9) Tired students may have trouble paying attention, remembering new information, and reacting quickly. (10) My brother once fell asleep at the dinner table. (11) Athletes who sleep less may also recover more slowly after practice.

(12) Some simple habits can help. (13) Keeping the same bedtime on weekends, putting phones away an hour before bed, and getting morning sunlight can all help.$q$, 'draft')
