values ('b6327a3d-000c-590f-9abf-2137d73175ee', 'wg8-narrative-writing-p01', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g8-narrative-writing'), null,
        '6-8', $q$The Robot That Would Not Turn$q$, $q$(1) The gym smelled like floor wax and nervous energy on the morning of the regional robotics competition. (2) My teammate Kenji and I had spent six weeks building a robot named Pebble, and today it had to push three foam blocks into a goal in under two minutes. (3) We set Pebble on the practice mat for one last test. (4) It rolled forward perfectly, but when it reached the first block, it spun in a slow circle instead of turning left. (5) Kenji groaned. (6) The gym was built in 1985 and has a scoreboard on the north wall. (7) I grabbed the laptop and scrolled through our code, line by line. (8) My hands were shaking so much that I could barely type.

(9) "Found it," I said at last. (10) One of us had typed a 9 where a 90 should have been, so Pebble was turning nine degrees instead of ninety. (11) I fixed the number and uploaded the program. (12) We carried Pebble to the competition table. (13) The judge blew a whistle, and Pebble rolled toward the first block. (14) It turned left, nudged the block into the goal, and went back for the second. (15) When the buzzer sounded, all three blocks sat in the goal with eleven seconds to spare.

(16) We didn't win first place, but that was okay.$q$, 'draft')
