   $q$The writer wants to slow the pacing at the most suspenseful moment by adding sensory detail. Where would this detail be most effective?$q$, $q$[{"text":"after sentence 2, explaining how the team chose the name Pebble","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"slows-wrong-moment"},{"text":"after sentence 11, describing the color and size of the laptop","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"after sentence 13, describing Pebble creeping toward the first block while the narrator holds her breath","is_correct":true},{"text":"after sentence 15, listing the robots built by the other teams","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"pacing-after-climax"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$after sentence 13, describing Pebble creeping toward the first block while the narrator holds her breath$q$, $q$Sentence 13 is the moment the fix is tested, when the reader wonders whether Pebble will turn, so slowing down there builds suspense. Details about the name in sentence 2 come before any tension exists.$q$, 'draft', 'b6327a3d-000c-590f-9abf-2137d73175ee')
