-- Passage wg8-narrative-writing-p02
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('356ed476-6dec-50d7-999d-eefe687ba364', 'wg8-narrative-writing-p02', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g8-narrative-writing'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Seeds in the Vacant Lot$q$, $q$(1) It started with a vacant lot. (2) For three years, the corner of Elm Street and Fourth Avenue had held nothing but weeds, broken bottles, and a sagging fence. (3) Malik walked past it every day on his way to school. (4) One afternoon in March, he noticed a small sign zip-tied to the fence: "Community Garden Meeting, Saturday, 10 a.m."

(5) On Saturday, Malik showed up and found only four other people. (6) Mrs. Delgado, who lived above the laundromat, held a clipboard. (7) A college student named Priya had brought a box of seed packets. (8) They spent the morning pulling weeds. (9) By noon, Malik's palms were blistered and his sneakers were caked with mud.

(10) The first sprouts appeared in late April. (11) Malik had planted a row of beans along the fence, and he checked on them every morning before school. (12) In July, the beans climbed all the way to the top of the fence. (13) Malik also likes to play basketball. (14) Mrs. Delgado said the garden was nice. (15) More neighbors joined every week.

(16) The garden was good.$q$, 'draft')
