   $q$Sentence 9 tells what Grandpa is thinking, which the first-person narrator cannot know. Which revision keeps the narrator's point of view?$q$, $q$[{"text":"You could tell that Grandpa thought I was bored out of my mind.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"second-person-shift"},{"text":"Grandpa felt tired of waiting and wanted to be home in his chair.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"pov-shift-unfixed"},{"text":"Grandpa thought I was bored, and he also wished he had come by himself.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"pov-shift-unfixed"},{"text":"Grandpa glanced at me and asked if I wanted to head back to the car.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Grandpa glanced at me and asked if I wanted to head back to the car.$q$, $q$The narrator can see Grandpa glance and hear his question, so the correct choice stays in first person. The other choices still report Grandpa's private thoughts or feelings, or switch to "you."$q$, 'draft', '4bde5af7-c78b-5cd5-874a-1185363bc282')
