   $q$Which sentence would best replace sentence 16 as a conclusion that shows the significance of the experience?$q$, $q$[{"text":"I got an A, which is the best grade anyone can get on a project.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"focus-on-grade"},{"text":"Textile mills were common in Massachusetts in the early 1900s.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"generic-fact-ending"},{"text":"Then I put the letters back in the box and forgot about them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-significance"},{"text":"When I finished reading Giulia's words aloud, the room was silent, and the project felt like a story I would keep telling.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$When I finished reading Giulia's words aloud, the room was silent, and the project felt like a story I would keep telling.$q$, $q$The correct choice shows the class's reaction and what the letters now mean to the narrator. Ending on the grade keeps the focus on the assignment instead of on Giulia and her story.$q$, 'draft', 'b8b6da68-3cce-5c31-a362-e882a6d91854')
