-- Passage wg8-narrative-writing-p07
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('a16a8458-1b5f-5b95-a034-e4a19bbd7b00', 'wg8-narrative-writing-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g8-narrative-writing'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Waiting for the Comet$q$, $q$(1) My neighbor, Mr. Achterberg, told me a comet would be visible for only three nights in October. (2) I had never seen a comet, so I begged my dad to drive us out of the city, where the sky would be darker. (3) We packed a borrowed telescope, two folding chairs, and a star map. (4) We parked in a field outside town.

(5) At first, all I could see were airplanes and one bright star that turned out to be a planet. (6) I pointed the telescope where the star map said the comet should be. (7) There was nothing. (8) I checked the map again. (9) My dad yawned. (10) He said we should go home. (11) I asked for five more minutes.

(12) Then I saw it. (13) It was a fuzzy smudge of light with a faint tail stretching away from it, like a thumbprint on a window. (14) I couldn't breathe. (15) Comets are made of ice, dust, and rock. (16) My dad leaned over to look, and for a long moment neither of us said anything.

(17) We drove home.$q$, 'draft')
