-- Passage wg8-paragraph-transitions-p06
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('e4fa83ee-f9dd-5ee5-aaf4-e036f0faa3d2', 'wg8-paragraph-transitions-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g8-paragraph-transitions'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Learning to Use the 3D Printer$q$, $q$(1) Last month, our class learned how to use the 3D printer in the school makerspace. (2) First, each student designed a simple object, such as a keychain or a phone stand, on a computer. (3) The printer heats a thin plastic thread until it melts. (4) Next, we saved the design as a special file that the printer could read. (5) The nozzle then lays down the melted plastic one thin layer at a time, building the object from the bottom up. (6) A small keychain took about forty minutes, while a phone stand took almost three hours.

(7) The makerspace also has a sewing machine that the drama club uses for costumes. (8) Some of our early prints came out lopsided because the bottom layer did not stick to the printer bed. (9) Our teacher showed us how to level the bed and wipe it clean before each print. (10) After that, almost every print came out smooth and even.$q$, 'draft')
