  ('21e7dbb8-8130-5494-9f1b-560431411437', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g8-paragraph-transitions'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Read the sentences: (A) Once the glue had dried, she sanded the rough corners. (B) Lina measured and cut four pieces of wood for her birdhouse. (C) Finally, she painted the roof bright blue. (D) Next, she glued the pieces together to form the walls. Which is the most logical order for these sentences?$q$, $q$[{"text":"B, D, A, C","is_correct":true},{"text":"B, D, C, A","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-finally"},{"text":"B, A, D, C","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-transition-cues"},{"text":"D, B, A, C","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-transition-cues"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$B, D, A, C$q$, $q$Lina must cut the wood first, then glue it ("Next"), then sand once the glue dries, and paint last ("Finally"). Order B, A, D, C is wrong because sentence A refers to glue that has dried, which cannot happen before the gluing in sentence D.$q$, 'draft', null)
