  ('cb87b944-53f7-5037-96c8-847f7f6d422a', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g8-paragraph-transitions'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Read: "The Elmwood Library's summer reading challenge kept kids reading all season. Participants logged their reading minutes on a chart at the front desk. Every five hundred minutes earned a ticket for an end-of-summer raffle. By August, children had read more than ten thousand minutes in total." Which sentence best concludes this paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Next year, the library may add a short story contest.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"new-idea-conclusion"},{"text":"Clearly, the challenge made summer a season of steady reading.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The raffle tickets were printed on bright orange paper.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"minor-detail-conclusion"},{"text":"Some children like reading comic books more than novels.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-conclusion"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Clearly, the challenge made summer a season of steady reading.$q$, $q$The correct sentence restates the main idea, that the challenge kept kids reading, and the ten thousand minutes support "Clearly." The sentence about a story contest brings in a new idea instead of wrapping up this one.$q$, 'draft', null)
