   $q$Read the sentence: "The reason why the bridge closed is because the inspectors found cracks." Which revision is the most concise and still clear?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The reason the bridge closed is because inspectors found cracks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"keeps-redundancy"},{"text":"Inspectors found cracks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"drops-key-meaning"},{"text":"Cracks, which inspectors found, are the reason why the bridge closed.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"keeps-wordiness"},{"text":"The bridge closed because inspectors found cracks.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The bridge closed because inspectors found cracks.$q$, $q$"The reason why ... is because" says the cause twice, so "because" alone is enough. The choice "The reason the bridge closed is because inspectors found cracks" removes "why" but still pairs "the reason" with "because."$q$, 'draft', null)
