   $q$The art club president wants to point out a problem in an email to all members without blaming one person. Which sentence does this best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Something happened with some stuff after a meeting.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-wording"},{"text":"Somebody really messed up the brushes, as usual.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"informal-style"},{"text":"The paintbrushes were not cleaned after Tuesday's meeting.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Jonah did not clean the paintbrushes after Tuesday's meeting.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"actor-focus-wrong-purpose"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The paintbrushes were not cleaned after Tuesday's meeting.$q$, $q$The passive voice states the problem clearly while leaving out who did it, which keeps the email tactful. Naming Jonah is direct and active, but it blames one member in front of everyone.$q$, 'draft', null)
