   $q$Read the sentence: "A decision was reached by the members of the robotics team to enter the regional competition." Which revision is active, concise, and keeps the meaning?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The regional competition was decided to be entered by the robotics team.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"still-passive"},{"text":"The members of the robotics team reached a decision that they would enter the regional competition.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"keeps-wordiness"},{"text":"The robotics team decided to enter the regional competition.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The robotics team made a decision about the regional competition.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"drops-key-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The robotics team decided to enter the regional competition.$q$, $q$The team is now the subject, and "decided to enter" replaces the long passive phrase. The choice "The robotics team made a decision about the regional competition" is active, but it no longer says what the team decided.$q$, 'draft', null)
